WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:04.491
Learn's comparison page
lists no variation in Azure

3
00:00:04.491 --> 00:00:07.838
Policy between commercial
Azure and Azure Government.

4
00:00:07.838 --> 00:00:12.205
But the fed-ramp initiatives exist
in separate versions for each cloud,

5
00:00:12.205 --> 00:00:17.238
as Cloud Boundary and Landing Zone notes,
and built-in definitions differ by cloud.

6
00:00:17.238 --> 00:00:19.997
That's why the guide lists
them by display name,

7
00:00:19.997 --> 00:00:23.701
and has you look each one up in the
cloud you're in, as the lab does.

8
00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:26.062
In G C C, the workbook's baseline,

9
00:00:26.062 --> 00:00:30.125
the commercial subscriptions
run Step 9 as written.

10
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:35.138
In Azure Government, use its own
initiative versions and definition names.

11
00:00:35.138 --> 00:00:40.238
And the guide lists assuming commercial
features in Azure Government as a danger of

12
00:00:40.238 --> 00:00:42.861
its own: a test the cloud
can't run is recorded

13
00:00:42.861 --> 00:00:45.840
as an environment decision,
not a failed control.
